{% if techniqueCatalogueForGeneration and techniqueCatalogueForGeneration.disciplines and techniqueCatalogueForGeneration.disciplines.length %}
Known world techniques available for optional initial learning. Only a technique's <id> is a valid <techniqueId>; a parent discipline's <id> must never be copied into <techniqueId>. This is an identity lookup, not permission to bypass use-time requirements. The server resolves full canonical mechanics from each exact technique ID.
<knownTechniqueCatalogue><disciplines>
{% for discipline in techniqueCatalogueForGeneration.disciplines %}<discipline><id>{{ discipline.id | xmlText }}</id><name>{{ discipline.name | xmlText }}</name><techniques>
{% for technique in discipline.techniques %}<technique><id>{{ technique.id | xmlText }}</id><name>{{ technique.name | xmlText }}</name>{% if technique.shortDescription %}<shortDescription>{{ technique.shortDescription | xmlText }}</shortDescription>{% endif %}</technique>
{% endfor %}</techniques></discipline>
{% endfor %}</disciplines></knownTechniqueCatalogue>
{% else %}
No existing public world techniques are listed for this prompt. Omit <startingTechniques> or leave it empty for every generated NPC; do not put a discipline, skill, invented ID or display name in <techniqueId>. A later initial-authoring step may create new techniques.
{% endif %}
